  "query_preview": "the Heat Advisory through Sunday with daily high \ntemperatures reaching the upper 90s to near 100 degrees. \n\nAlthough heat index values on Sunday are more marginal near 100 \ndegrees, the record or near record breaking temperatures that \nare 10-15 degrees above normal combined with high humidity\nlevels will continue to elevate heat-related health impacts. \nWith an increase in weekend outdoor actives late in the season, \nthe heat impacts will be greater than normal despite what the \ncriteria may suggest. In fact, multiple records are likely to be\ntied if not broken over the coming days.\n\nAs for any relief in the short term, there is a 20-30% chance \nof an isolated shower or thunderstorm this afternoon near and \nnorth of I-64 due to a stationary sfc frontal boundary, but \ncoverage will be sparse at best. Rain chances in the north are \neven lower Thursday into Friday, but non-zero as the \naformentioned boundary remains in the vicinity. It will not be \nuntil Monday into Tuesday when true relief from the heat and \nhumidity arrives with high temperatures trending into the 80s as\na cold front approaches. Daily isolated showers and \nthunderstorms will also be possible each day.",
